Z||000000||chris6878||01-06-2000||03:28 AM||||get this... I filled her up today.. the gauge is constantly sitting at 1/4 of a tank... after pumping.. i turn the ingnition on.. and the gauge moves alway to a little over the full gauge... but then went right back to the 1/4 tank mark in a few seconds... hmmmmmm???<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||DJRice||01-06-2000||10:16 AM||||Sounds like a short or a bad sending unit.  I would vote for a bad sending unit if after you filled it up it jumped to full and then dropped to 1/4. If it does this regardless of how much gas is in the tank, that is probably a short.  You might start by checking the 3 wire connector that runs the fuel pump and gauge.  It is on the firewall near the 2 bundles of wire that head into the cabin.  The believe the wires are black, brown, and lavender.||||reg||1
Z||000002||chris6878||01-06-2000||04:20 PM||||thanks.. i will check today...   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000003||David Gamache||01-07-2000||01:34 AM||||I had the same problem and when I removed the gas tank the sending unit was literally falling apart.||||reg||1
